  "final_answer": "I have successfully retrieved the simplified polynomial from Wolfram Alpha. The image alt text in the DOM clearly shows the result.\n\n## Answer\n\nThe simplified form of **x^5 - 20x^4 + 163x^3 - 676x^2 + 1424x - 1209** is:\n\n**(x - 4)^5 + 3(x - 4)^3 + 7**\n\n### Verification\n\nWolfram Alpha reduced the polynomial from 6 terms to just 3 terms by recognizing it as a polynomial centered around x = 4. We can verify by expanding:\n\n- (x - 4)^5 = x^5 - 20x^4 + 160x^3 - 640x^2 + 1280x - 1024\n- 3(x - 4)^3 = 3x^3 - 36x^2 + 144x - 192\n- + 7\n\n**Sum:** x^5 - 20x^4 + (160 + 3)x^3 + (-640 - 36)x^2 + (1280 + 144)x + (-1024 - 192 + 7)\n       = x^5 - 20x^4 + 163x^3 - 676x^2 + 1424x - 1209 ✓\n\nThe original 6-term polynomial was successfully simplified into a more compact 3-term expression centered at x = 4.",
